   syntax: #history
   Shows you the last bunch of commands that you've typed.
   You can do history substitution with these:

   !<# of line to repeat> <additional text>

   ex: #history              <-- could show something like this:

   8  say Hello there hon!
   7  say eh?  no--i didn't take your sword--gogmagog did.
   6  say i don't recall at this moment.
   5  tell gogmagog i told her you did it!
   4  n
   3  e
   2  open door
   1  tell cylia gog did it!
   0  #history

   Then if she didn't believe us, we could repeat it:

   ex: !1                   <-- will repeat history entry 1

